**Working as a prototype**

- A complete visual identity and a readable long-scroll page.
- Filter + search + empty state.
- Company dossier as a modal, with body scroll lock.
- Responsive layout that actually reflows (not just a squeezed desktop).
- Some a11y: `sr-only`, `aria-modal`, reduced-motion, labelled search.

**Painted on**

- “Verified” and “SYNCED” — no pipeline behind them.
- Newsletter — local success only (README admits this).
- Bookmarks — write-only.
- Company index — six rows, no search, no permalinks, no story join.
- “04 MIN READ” on the lead story — there is no article body.

**Small product/engineering holes if this stays a real site**

- Dossier does not close on Escape and has no focus trap.
- Story cards are not themselves links; only the source chip is.
- No router, so a company or story cannot be shared.
- Google Fonts loaded from the CSS `@import` (render-blocking, privacy).
- Entire app is one component; any next feature will fight that file.

